The church comes from Houdini into Unreal Engine 5.8, with heightmaps made in Copernicus. The scene has only three materials, each with a 2,048 px texture. They are the white paint, the window and wood, and the roof tiles, a trim sheet. The window and wood, in variations A and B, share one texture with the stair. On a test, the render costs about 0.9 seconds per frame at 3,360 x 1,440 in 21:9 at 24 fps.
